WEBVTT

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.850
Good morning, Kei!

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:08.110
This time, I've got a message from Friday,
July 14th, which is yesterday for you.

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.910
I believe you made an important
appointment before yesterday.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.890
You were going to drink tea with
some cutie on Saturday the 15th.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:19.370
I'm giving you this wake-up call
so that you don't oversleep.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.760
And now, it's time for our pop idol,
Haruki Misora, to take the stage!

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.240
Um, Kei, are you awake?

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.400
Please don't be late for tomorrow.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.380
You heard her, Kei. Isn't it about time you wake up?

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.600
What do you want, Kei? It's so early...

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.690
Payback for disrupting my sleep.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.570
Sorry about that. That must've been bothersome.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.700
That's an annoying ability.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.530
It's a pretty strong ability despite it
only being able to send voice messages.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.290
I can't resist it no matter what.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.040
Oh, I just remembered.
I added another cat to my collection.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.380
A wind chime, huh?
I haven't seen one of those in a while.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.040
Want me to lend it to you?

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.800
I like hearing wind chimes once
in a while when I least expect it.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.170
Much like finding a rainbow.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.300
Wouldn't it be wonderful if there was a tool that
could allow you to see a rainbow at any time?

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.390
Isn't there a bit of charm
in noticing them once in a while?

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.400
It's kind of sad for a wind chime to keep
ringing where no one will notice it.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.900
For all you know, the wind chime might
enjoy its own gracefully lone sound.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.320
Nice to meet you. I'm Asai Kei.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.910
And she's Haruki Misora.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.950
I'm Murase Youka.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.490
I've come on a referral from Mr. Tsushima.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.160
Asai, you're a high school student, right?

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.670
Yes, I'm a first-year.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.670
Why are you doing the Bureau's work?

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.800
Because I'm in that kind of club.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.670
It's called the Ashiharabashi Service Club.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.590
"Service Club"?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.890
We're being monitored by the Bureau.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.140
Do you possess a dangerous ability?

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.180
My memory is kind of good, that's all.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:32.850
Murase, I heard that your request
is to search for your lost cat, but...

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.650
I already found my cat.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.690
He's been run over by a car.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:41.200
My request is for you to revive my dead cat.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.660
I see.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.990
By the way, Murase,

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.700
are you prepared to kill three days'
worth of the world's time for your cat?

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.580
What do you mean by that?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.720
The cat's name is Mike.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.100
She's had him for six months.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.220
Yesterday morning, on Friday the 14th,

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.560
he was run over by a car in front
of a bakery in the shopping district.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.730
Doesn't that seem a little strange?

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.060
What about it is strange?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.650
The Bureau doesn't get involved
in non-ability incidents, right?

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.650
Yeah.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:25.990
The Bureau only acts in cases where
problems involving special abilities arise.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:29.490
Also, there was too little time
between the accident and the request.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:32.160
<i>She found out about the accident yesterday morning,</i>

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.330
<i>and I heard about the request
yesterday during lunch break.</i>

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:40.550
<i>In just a few hours, we were given both the Bureau's
authorization and Tsushima's instructions.</i>

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.670
<i>That's way too quick.</i>

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.050
What are we going to do?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.720
We'll save the cat, of course.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.510
Let's gather some information first.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.600
I'll contact Hitsuuchi.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.930
Could you go check out
the scene of the accident for me?

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:53.940
Sure.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:59.610
The number you have reached
is no longer in service.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.400
Please check the number and—

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.370
The number you have reached is no longer in—

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.960
The number you have reached is—

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:26.550
The number you have reached is—

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.220
The number you have... reached is...

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.640
This is Asai. I'd like to ask you something.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.190
...no longer in service.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.400
Please check the number and...

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.650
It's been a while, Kei.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.650
Would you quit with this system, Hitsuuchi?

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:46.820
No way.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:50.160
What'll happen if my voice gives away my identity?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.830
Are you looking for a cat today?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:52.830
Yeah.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.370
Let me introduce you to a cat expert.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.670
Nonoh Seika, a first-year at Oomiya High School.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.670
Her ability allows her to distribute information.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.630
However, it works only on cats.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:08.130
When it comes to cats, there's no one more knowledgeable and loving than she is.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.100
On her days off, she naps with
the cats at the Kamisaki Shrine.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.850
Got it. Thank you.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.850
By the way, Kei, do you know what a MacGuffin is?

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:20.350
"MacGuffin"? I know the dictionary definition of it.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:23.360
I see. Well, if you don't know, then it's fine. See ya.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.360
Here, have one.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.650
Thanks.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.200
It seems the shop assistant didn't see it happen.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:37.870
But he said he might've heard the sound of the
car braking sometime between 8 and 9 o'clock.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.080
The time matches.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.960
Also, Hitsuuchi asked me about a MacGuffin.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.210
What's a "MacGuffin"?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.050
It's a film and theater term.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:51.760
It's an item that serves as a trigger
for the protagonist in the story.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.180
If the protagonist is a thief,
then it's a precious stone he'd be after.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.970
If he's in a gang, then it's wads of cash.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.020
But you can switch the items around.

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.810
Basically, the possible objectives of a protagonist

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.860
are commonly known as a "MacGuffin."

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.860
Is it related to this incident?

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.320
Beats me.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.780
We had plans to come to the festival at night...

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:12.950
Let's come here at night, too.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:19.540
You saved three days ago at 12:59.
It's 12:40 right now.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.540
We don't have much time left, huh?

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.010
I'd like to ask you about a cat
that was in an accident.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.520
We might be able to save that cat.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.790
<i>Just 13 more minutes. We're cutting it close.</i>

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.760
Are you Nonoh?

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:14.680
Morning.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.390
You said someone was in an accident?

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:20.680
A cat with gray fur, blue eyes, and a crooked tail.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.980
He belonged to a person named Murase.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.980
How long did this Murase person have that cat?

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.730
About six months.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.240
There isn't a cat like that in Sakurada.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.950
This cat was run over in front
of a bakery yesterday morning.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:42.500
I certainly haven't seen him around lately.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.790
Something probably happened, then.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:49.210
Even if he did get into an accident,
how can you save him?

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:52.840
We have an ability that allows
us to—or rather, she does.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:55.720
Would you like some?

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.220
No thanks. I'm good.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:05.020
If you happen to visit again, please bring
some cream puffs from Sangatsudou.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.060
<i>We're out of time.</i>

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.730
Anyway, we'd like you to tell us about that cat.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.530
I can't fall asleep immediately.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.700
You can't use your ability when you're awake?

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:19.870
I need to be in a clear state of mind that is free
of any thought so that I can forget myself.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.660
Sleeping is the quickest and easiest way to do that.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.120
If you sleep, you'll know where the cat was, right?

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.460
Not if it's dead.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.000
Let me try sleeping.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.250
Sing me a lullaby.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.460
Haruki?

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.000
Huh?

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.630
Should I sing?

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:37.680
It's time to reset.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:47.900
It's 12:59 on a Wednesday. The date is July 12th.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.110
It seems you did a reset.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:54.280
Looks like we have to look for a cat.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.490
Why did you reset?

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.700
Three days from now, on Saturday the 15th,

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:03.160
we went to meet a person named Murase
Youka under Mr. Tsushima's instructions.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:07.370
And we accepted her request to save
her cat, which was run over by a car.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.670
Got it.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.090
Thanks.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.380
Sure.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.560
Searching for a cat, huh?

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:29.690
Well then, I'm counting on you.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.940
That's it?

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.150
Is there a problem?

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.030
It's a request you'll give me two days later.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.650
I'm busy with all sorts of things, too, you know.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:39.780
I can't stand students who play hooky.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:46.040
Since you've reset, I'll be doing the same work
I've already done for the next three days, right?

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.910
Yeah, pretty much.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:49.960
That's depressing.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:54.340
You don't even remember doing the work,
so in reality, this is your first time.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.670
It's a matter of how I feel.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:59.010
By the way, do you know what a MacGuffin is?

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.470
A "MacGuffin"?

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.010
Hitsuuchi asked me about it before the reset.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.890
I see.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.560
Well, it's not like I'd know
something that he doesn't know.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.390
Hey, did you know?

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.770
I heard that a vampire appears
at the haunted mountain!

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.020
A vampire?

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.860
Wasn't that rumor popular a few years ago?

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.110
Wanna come with me to look for the vampire?

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.860
<i>This must be Kei's second time
hearing this conversation.</i>

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:25.660
<i>But he faithfully recreates
the conversation from the first time.</i>

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:29.120
<i>He keeps acting like he's listening for the first time.</i>

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.790
Go with the U-Research people for that.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.130
"U-Research"?

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.460
It's a club that researches the unidentified.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.250
I'm a member.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:43.300
<i>After what happened two years ago,
Kei hates changing the future unnecessarily.</i>

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:56.520
What kind of person is that cat-lover Nonoh?

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:00.950
She's cat-like, but she doesn't end her
sentences with "meow" when she talks.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.740
Do you like things like that?

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.240
Things like what?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.530
Ending sentences with "meow."

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.490
Oh, yeah, I think it's cute.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.870
Nice weather we're having today, meow.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.630
Yeah... um...

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.420
What's wrong, meow?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.420
Sorry, I lied.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:20.670
Please speak normally.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.010
Is that so? All right, then.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.430
You should value yourself a little more.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:28.510
If you say so, I'll try my best to.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:31.520
For now, you should do something
about that thought process.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.020
You sure say some complicated things.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.320
Nonoh.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:42.400
And you are?

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:45.160
We met in three days. My name's Kei Asai.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:51.080
So basically, what you two are saying
is that you know the future.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.410
Well, that's about right.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:54.710
Whatever.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:58.750
What's really important is that
you know what my favorite food is.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:03.630
As things stand right now, a cat is going to die
in a car accident the day after tomorrow.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:07.720
How long has this Murase person had that cat?

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:10.260
Next Saturday, you asked the same question.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:13.270
I happen to know something about that cat.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:16.100
But the cat I know of is a stray.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.480
Do you know where that stray cat is now?

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.320
Let's try and find out.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:26.070
Kei, are we still going to
go through with this request?

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.870
There's no reason for us to quit.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:31.490
But Murase might be lying.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.000
Did that cat really belong to her?

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.830
It being a stray or not makes no difference.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.830
If it's going to get into an accident, let's save it.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:43.130
Isn't there a possibility that
Murase is trying to use us?

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.920
Of course there is.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:48.970
She might've wanted us to use your
reset ability for some other reason.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:51.640
Is it okay to continue fulfilling this request?

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:54.310
We're talking about a possibility here.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:57.270
We can't dismiss it just because of that.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.770
It's no good.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.900
What's no good?

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.440
It seems he's sleeping right now.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.650
Is that a problem?

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:11.950
My ability is gaining access to a cat's senses.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:15.580
So even if I share a cat's senses with it while
it's sleeping, I won't know what's going on.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.750
I see.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.670
If you want me to, I could try again later.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.210
Please do.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:24.050
Would you please call us
once you find out where it is?

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:28.050
Sure. I'll be more than happy
to do it if it saves the cat.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.430
There's a festival on Saturday, right?

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:32.810
Would you like to go together?

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.010
That's right.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:36.560
This request should wrap up before that time.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.600
I need to get a yukata for it.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.900
I was thinking of buying a new one.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.110
Isn't last year's fine? It looked good on you.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.570
No matter what I wear,
you always say it looks good on me.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.620
You must not be into girl's clothing.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.450
I like stuff like miniskirts.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.870
Preferably, red plaid skirts.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.540
But you'd hate it if I actually wore one.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.420
That's because that'd be extreme for you to wear.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.500
But you just said you like it.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.250
I did say that, but...

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:08.220
Should I get a red plaid miniskirt, then?

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.340
You don't have to.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:13.390
I only like it if some girl I passed
by happened to wear one.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.720
Kei, that's—

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:15.930
This is Asai.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.730
Hey, Kei. What do you need today?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:22.100
We reset after I got information from you.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:26.190
I was looking for the cat,
and I got introduced to Nonoh Seika.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.530
I see.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.860
So why did you go through
the trouble of calling me this time?

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.910
I've got something I want to ask.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.910
Do you know Murase Youka?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:37.370
Disclosing information about her is prohibited.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.250
In other words, you do know her.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.290
I already said I can't talk about that.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.040
What's a MacGuffin?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.750
Disclosing information on that is also prohibited.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:51.630
Did the same person instruct you
to conceal information regarding those two?

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:52.840
That's a secret.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:56.720
You seem to be doing well right now.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.140
What makes you think that?

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:01.850
You're suspecting a relation between
the MacGuffin and Murase Youka.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:04.940
Naturally, they shouldn't be related in any way.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:07.400
Is it okay for you to be saying this to me?

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.360
I'm almost crossing the line.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:14.660
Though I don't know anything
about the nature of the MacGuffin.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.530
See ya.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:18.040
How did it go?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:22.290
We shouldn't be distrustful of people.
There's no point since our hands are tied.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:27.960
Yes?

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.960
He had been abducted!

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.970
"He"? You mean the cat?

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.590
He was kidnapped.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.640
He's been taken somewhere by a stranger.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.100
Where is he now?

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:42.680
Sorry. I know nothing about the things
the cat personally doesn't understand.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.440
I don't mind if it's just what you know.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:49.820
He was abducted at around 3 p.m today.
It happened in front of Nishi Ward Park.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:52.110
It's immediately after the reset.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.900
Is the cat inside a room?

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:54.950
It seems like it.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.820
I could see a bed and a desk.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:17:00.450
There was a framed picture of
a young man on top of the desk.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.790
Anyway, that means the cat is alive, right?

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:03.660
Yeah.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.540
Please continue gathering information.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:06.670
It'll be all right.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:10.250
If he's still okay, I'm sure it means
the guy doesn't intend to hurt him.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.380
That's true. I'll call you later.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:18.430
<i>Why was the cat abducted?</i>

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:21.970
<i>If her objective was to make us reset,
then she should've achieved her goal.</i>

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:24.520
<i>There's no need to do anything unnecessary.</i>

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:26.140
<i>So why?</i>

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.530
Do you know the story about the hole in the wall?

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:33.570
Hole?

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:38.820
It's not just any hole. It's shaped just
like a hand with five distinct fingers.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:42.120
People say they saw it on the
residential street yesterday evening.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:46.000
What's more, they said the hole suddenly
closed up right before their eyes.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.370
What do you think, Asai?

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.750
<i>I didn't hear about this before the reset.</i>

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:55.340
Um... I'm sure an ability like that exists.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:58.590
What?! It's a ghost-like story!

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.010
You sure are a spoilsport.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.600
Ghosts, huh?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:05.140
By the way, have you guys
ever heard of a MacGuffin?

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:07.520
"MacGuffin"? What's that?

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.150
A rumor or something.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.190
I don't have the slightest idea.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.730
Want me to ask my friends in U-Research?

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.690
They might know if it has
something to do with the occult.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.160
That'd be great. I appreciate it.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:22.580
<i>Is there someone else who has the ability
to preserve their memory from a reset?</i>

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:27.830
Hello?

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:30.670
It's no good. I can't use my ability.

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.210
You're unable to sleep?

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:35.670
Yeah. I've been using my ability
too much for the past day.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.760
Is there anything I can help with?

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.470
Please talk to me about something.
Anything will do.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.100
Let's talk about something trivial
that will make me sleepy.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:47.560
Okay, then, what would you
want to be if you were reborn?

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:50.190
Well, a humongous tree would be good.

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:50.980
Why?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.400
As a tree, cats would climb up on my body.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:57.780
Then they could sit on my branches
and look at things in the distance.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:01.240
Since I'd be a tall tree,
they'd be able to see everything far away.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:04.240
The world is peaceful, and it often has clear skies.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.000
So we'll look at that together.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:11.790
Rain or shine, the cat will climb up on me,

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:17.050
and I'll just support it as it looks
at everything in the distance.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:18.880
That's a great answer.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:23.140
Asai, what would you want to be if you were reborn?

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.970
I'd want to be God.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.640
I won't put each and every person through trials.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.150
I'll be a God that isn't distrustful of humans.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.150
I'll give bread to the hungry,

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:38.650
and make sad people happy.

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:44.280
I could even put a rainbow up in the distant
sky for you, the tree, and the cat to see.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.470
I could see just a little.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.930
He ate high-grade cat food and is happy.

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.310
So the cat is safe, right?

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.270
Yeah, it might've just been picked up.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:13.480
That's good to hear.

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:14.480
I'll call you later.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:19.650
Kei, it's been 24 hours since we last did a reset.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:21.820
Haruki, tell me the time.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:25.410
59 minutes and 10 seconds. 11... 12...

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:26.280
Save.

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:27.410
Save.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:35.670
It's Thursday, July 13th. The time is 12:59:15.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.420
It seems you still haven't done the second reset.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:43.340
Well, then, let's eat lunch.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:45.050
Is the cat okay?

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.680
For now, yeah.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:50.310
Tomorrow morning, let's go to the site
where the cat will get into an accident.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.560
I'll bring black tea in a thermos.

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:55.440
Let's have some freshly baked bread together.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.750
Do you think the cat will come?

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.330
It's touch and go.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:18.290
A voice!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:20.590
I hear a voice.

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.050
"Voice"? You mean the cat's?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.300
There's no mistake. It's him!

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:40.230
Um... Nice to meet you, I guess?

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:44.950
Wait!

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:46.820
Upper body. Gravity.

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:50.370
She flew!

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:02.130
You rescued the cat, so isn't that a good thing?

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:03.800
It's a done deal.

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:06.800
What was Murase's objective?

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:08.840
Who cares what it was.

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:10.970
You fulfilled the request.

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:12.890
No one's unhappy.

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:15.390
What more are you asking for?

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:18.690
Then, I don't have to do anything anymore, right?

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.310
Just one thing.

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:22.820
When's the last time you saved?

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:24.570
Yesterday, during the day.

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:27.650
Sorry, but for the time being, don't reset.

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:30.320
Not until the very end of the three days, if you can.

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:31.660
Yes, sir.

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:36.580
<i>Which means there might be something else, huh?</i>

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:41.080
<i>This time, we reset to save the cat.</i>

00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:44.840
<i>But that reset made something unexpected happen.</i>

00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:53.760
<i>What kind of objective did
she have to make that request?</i>

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:57.600
<i>Why did Mr. Tsushima approve of it?</i>

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:03.940
Good morning, Kei!

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:08.650
This time, I've got a message from Friday,
July 14th, which is yesterday for you.

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:09.610
I believe you made an important
appointment before yesterday.

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:12.030
That appointment was reset, you know.

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:13.740
You were going to drink tea with
some cutie on Saturday the 15th.

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:16.040
Um... Morning?
You were going to drink tea with
some cutie on Saturday the 15th.

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:16.410
I'm giving you this wake-up call
so that you don't oversleep.
Um... Morning?

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:18.290
I'm giving you this wake-up call
so that you don't oversleep.

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:19.910
Morning...
I'm giving you this wake-up call
so that you don't oversleep.

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:24.210
And now, it's time for our pop idol,
Haruki Misora, to take the stage!

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:27.760
We found Minami's body.

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:28.340
She was alive before the reset.
We found Minami's body.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:29.260
She was alive before the reset.

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:29.840
He goes by "Hitsuuchi."
She was alive before the reset.

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:30.970
He goes by "Hitsuuchi."

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:31.430
He was killed.

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:32.300
I still did something bad.
He was killed.

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:33.600
I still did something bad.

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:34.680
Do you know what a MacGuffin is?

00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:35.220
I decided to kill you both.
Do you know what a MacGuffin is?

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:36.720
I decided to kill you both.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:47.570
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:55.080
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:55.660 --> 00:24:00.540
Life is but a dream we never wake up from

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:08.630
We repeat it over and over, praying for salvation

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:14.180
I kept waiting endlessly for your signal

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:21.390
To make sure you wouldn't disappear all by yourself

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:25.900
Ah, it doesn't matter where I am or what I'm doing

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:29.610
My heart can't go against your will

00:24:29.610 --> 00:24:35.240
So I'd follow you even to the ends of the world

00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:42.370
I fell in love with you at the dawn of our new world

00:24:42.370 --> 00:24:49.000
But we kept pushing the hand of the clock backwards

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:56.050
And lost not only time, but our smiles as well

00:24:56.050 --> 00:25:00.140
You're the one who brought it back

00:25:00.140 --> 00:25:07.020
And taught me that even lies can be meaningful
